      "message": "That would complicate code on the device, which I think takes priority when it comes to simplification -- less chances to break devices.\n\nWe could make apex\u0027es know whether they are updatable, but that requires on device changes. (Or, provide a template of jars as you previously suggested, which again complicates the logic.) Also, splitting the PRODUCT_BOOT_JARS in make.\n\nBtw, i18n comes after all /system/ and /system_ext/ jars now (not in between ext.jar and telephony.jar). Honestly, it would simplify this a lot, if we made i18n part of PRODUCT_UPDATABLE_BOOT_JARS, which I was going to start a conversation on about later.\n\nI don\u0027t fully follow last two points. What configuration are we talking about here?",
